WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.836
Per cent means 'out of 100'.

2
00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:11.923
This grid has 100 squares.

3
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.790
25 squares are coloured. That is 25%.

4
00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:24.275
The key trick: find 10% first.

5
00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.682
The whole £80 is 100%.

6
00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:36.022
Split it into 10 equal parts. Each part is 10%.

7
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.783
To find 10%, divide by 10. £80 divided by 10 equals £8.

8
00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:49.043
20% is two parts: £16.

9
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.819
Percentage increase: the amount gets bigger.

10
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.633
Start with £80. That is 100%.

11
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.897
Find 20%: that is £16. Add it on.

12
00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:11.978
£80 + £16 equals £96.

13
00:01:13.967 --> 00:01:16.661
Percentage decrease: the amount gets smaller.

14
00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:23.559
Start with £50. 10% is £5.

15
00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:27.319
30% is three parts: £15.

16
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.193
Take £15 away.

17
00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:37.929
Fifty pounds minus fifteen pounds is thirty-five pounds.

18
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.315
Using a calculator? There is a shortcut.

19
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.015
Increase by 20%: you end up with 120%.

20
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.762
120% is 1.2. So multiply by 1.2.

21
00:01:57.733 --> 00:02:00.984
Decrease by 30%: you keep 70%.

22
00:02:02.967 --> 00:02:07.193
70% is 0.7. So multiply by 0.7.

23
00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:16.278
Find the percentage. Then add it or take it away.
